  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancement of M&amp;E System in the Roads Administration</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The proposed IDF grant aims at enhancing the results-oriented monitoring and evaluation system currently used in the Roads Administration in Kazakhstan. Specifically,  the grant will be used to assess the existing M&amp;E system used by the Roads Administration and prepare a strategy for its improvement, and  assist in the implementation of the strategy through hands-on expert advice, in particular in the area of project management. It will eventually target the scaling up of successful M&amp;E practices as developed under the South West Roads Project and other IFI supported projects. TF093848 The proposed IDF grant aims at enhancing the performance monitoring and evaluation systems of the Roads Administration. Specifically, the main development objective is two-pronged:  (i) assess the existing M&amp;E system used by the Roads Administration and prepare a strategy for its improvement, and (ii) assist in the implementation of the strategy through hands-on expert advice, with particular focus on project management. Proposed focal areas for project management include construction management, and project supervision related to fiduciary and governance aspects.  The proposed IDF grant aims at enhancing the performance monitoring and evaluation systems of the Roads Administration.</narrative>
  </description>
